For a hypothetical semiconductor with $n$-type doping and $E_{g}=1 \mathrm{eV}$ while $E_{d}=0.9 \mathrm{eV}$, the conductivity at room temperature $\left(25^{\circ} \mathrm{C}\right)$ is $100 \Omega^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{~m}^{-1}$. Calculate the conductivity at $30^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$.
Express the answer in this unit: \Omega^{-1} \cdot \mathrm{m}^{-1}

Before the final answer line, give a concise worked solution with the governing equation, substitution with units, and the calculation.

Given that at 20 °C a Cu–0.1 wt% Si alloy has a resistivity of ρ₍₂₀ °C₎=23.6×10⁻⁹ Ω·m, and that the temperature coefficient of resistivity of copper (and its dilute alloys) is α=0.00393 °C⁻¹, estimate the resistivity of the Cu–0.1 wt% Si alloy at 100 °C.
Express the answer in this unit: \Omega \cdot \mathrm{m}

Before the final answer line, give a concise worked solution with the governing equation, substitution with units, and the calculation.

Calculate the magnetic moment of an isolated $\mathrm{Mn}^{2+}$ cation, assuming that the orbital angular momentum is quenched, that is, $L=0$.
Express the answer in this unit: \mu_{B}

Before the final answer line, give a concise worked solution with the governing equation, substitution with units, and the calculation.

Iron oxide (FeO) has the rock salt crystal structure and a density of $5.70 \mathrm{~g} / \mathrm{cm}^{3}$, determine the unit cell edge length.

Reference:
$$
\begin{aligned}
& \sum A{\mathrm{Fe}}=A{\mathrm{Fe}}=55.85 \mathrm{~g} / \mathrm{mol} \\
& \sum A{\mathrm{O}}=A{\mathrm{O}}=16.00 \mathrm{~g} / \mathrm{mol}
\end{aligned}
$$
Express the answer in this unit: nm

Before the final answer line, give a concise worked solution with the governing equation, substitution with units, and the calculation.
